                <pb facs="0585" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg579"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 24th
                    September last I have the honor in accordance with instructions which I have
                    received from my Government to transmit for your information copy of a dispatch
                    which has been addressed by the Earl of Rosebery to Her Majesty’s consul in
                    Samoa, containing instructions for his guidance with respect to the audit of the
                    accounts of the municipality and the Samoan Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Michael H.
                    Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
